  "fixes": {
    "P2-B2": {
      "change": "the minimum computation and the absolute SetReadDeadline application are serialized under the SAME deadline mutex (applyEffectiveDeadlineLocked called while holding deadlineMu; the lock is never held across a Read). A concurrent cancellation can no longer be undone by a stale assembly apply, and a concurrent clear can no longer remove the active assembly cap",
      "coverage": "real net.Pipe socket probe (NewTargetLockCommitAmbiguityDeadlineProbe) sharing the exact adapter path: 25 rounds of competing caller-update vs apply must settle on the expired minimum (blocked real-socket read returns os.ErrDeadlineExceeded; a stale future apply would hang), plus clear-during-assembly and mid-read clear must keep the cap (bounded cap deadline on the real socket)"
    },
    "P2-B3": {
      "change": "both stall selects observe brokenCh and return a fail-closed transport error PROMPTLY; ControlFeedServerError also wakes stalled readers (same wake signal as byte feeds, with the actual-data check); added break-while-stalled and queued-error-wake completion proofs in the lane",
      "coverage": "break while stalled finishes the reader promptly (no 30s cap wait) with the 6 partial bytes consumed and no WITHHELD; a queued EOF wakes the stalled reader boundedly"
    }
  },
